    "result_text": "You can now record a tax number on a client, and it shows on the client's page and on their invoices. `bin/e2e` passes (1/1).\n\nOne note: the task said \"OfficeFloor server\", but this app is a plain Spring Boot app (only the Java package is named `net.officefloor`). I built the server side with ordinary Spring, as `CLAUDE.md` says.\n\n**Database:** a new migration, `V34__client_tax_number.sql`, adds an optional `tax_number` column (up to 50 characters) to `client`. Existing clients have none.\n\n**Server:**\n- Clients have a new `taxNumber` field. It is accepted when adding or editing a client and returned with the client. Blank values are saved as \"none\", and there's a 50-character limit, the same rules as phone number.\n- The invoice detail response now includes `clientTaxNumber`.\n- The test seed endpoint accepts `taxNumber` for clients.\n\n**Front end:**\n- **Client page:** shows the number as `client-tax-number`, or \"Not tax registered\" (`client-tax-number-none`) when there isn't one.\n- **Invoice page:** shows \"Client tax number\" (`invoice-client-tax-number`) only when the client has one.\n- **Add-client and edit-client forms:** an optional \"Tax number\" field (`client-form-tax-number` and `client-edit-form-tax-number`), with error messages under matching `-error` IDs.\n\nI didn't rename or remove any existing `data-testid`. The test only covers displaying the number. Adding or editing it through the forms hasn't been tested by me or by the spec.",
